.TH INVF-CONVERT 8 "2026-11" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf\-convert \- convert an ext4 image into an InvariantFS volume, and verify
the result path by path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf\-convert convert
.I src\-image
.I dst\-image
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B invf\-convert verify
.I src
.I dst
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B invf\-convert source\-map
.I src\-image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B convert
asks the ext4fs codecpack what the source\(aqs bytes are (its
.B classify
table: meta_structure, garbage, member), reads the source through a
read\-only loop mount, and imports the whole tree into a fresh volume:
regular files, directories, symlinks, special nodes and hardlinks (one
inode with nlink > 1), with mode, uid, gid, mtime at nanosecond precision
and every extended attribute the source carries. It then runs the engine\(aqs
own gates on the result
.RB ( invf\-fsck " and " invf\-verify\ \-\-deep )
and cross\-checks the import against the pack\(aqs member enumeration, inode by
inode.
.PP
Anything the volume cannot represent aborts the run by name (exit 3) and
removes the destination: a silent skip is data loss that no checker can
find.
.B verify
mounts both ends (loop, read\-only, and the FUSE daemon) and compares every
path: presence, type, size, mode, uid, gid, mtime (seconds and
nanoseconds), BLAKE3 of the logical content, symlink targets, nlink, device
numbers, the hardlink partition and every extended attribute.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pack\-dir=\fIDIR\fR
The ext4fs codecpack directory whose
.I bin/ext4fs
is executed. Default
.RB $ \fIINVFS_CONVERT_PACK\fR ,
else
.IR <repo>/tools/codecpacks/ext4fs.codecpack .
.TP
.B \-\-size=\fIGB\fR
Destination size. The default is
.IR content " + " 20\ KiB\ per\ inode " + " max(128\ MiB,\ 5%)\ ,
floored at the source image\(aqs own size.
.TP
.B \-\-meta\-frac=\fIN\fR
Sets
.B INVFS_META_FRAC
for
.BR invf\-mkfs .
Root filesystems want 16.
.TP
.B \-\-fold\-every=\fIN\fR
Fold the metadata delta every N created files (default 8192; 0 never
folds). A conversion that leaves the whole import in the delta log cannot
be compacted later on a tight volume.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-partial
Keep the destination image when the run fails.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gates
Skip
.B invf\-fsck
and
.B invf\-verify \-\-deep.
.TP
.B \-\-mount\-root=\fIDIR\fR
Where the loop and FUSE mounts are created.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-diffs=\fIN\fR
.B verify
only: print at most N differences (default 200; the count is always exact).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_CONVERT_PACK
Default codecpack directory.
.TP
.B INVFS_CONVERT_REAL_IMG
.BR tools/test\-convert\-ext4.sh
only: a real ext4 rootfs image for the real\-world leg
.IR ( INVFS_CONVERT_REAL=1 ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B convert:
0 converted and gated; 3 refused (an unsupported source, or a path the
volume cannot represent — nothing is left behind); 2 the run itself failed.
.B verify:
0 identical; 1 differences were found; 2 the comparison could not run.
.SH NOTES
Requires root: the source is loop\-mounted read\-only, and a root filesystem
contains files an ordinary user cannot read. Phase 0 only — the destination
is an ordinary new image; converting in place on the device that holds the
source is not implemented. See
.I impl_docs/CONVERT\-DESIGN.md
in the source tree for the phase\-1 design, its commit set and its crash
matrix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf\-import (8),
.BR invf\-mkfs (8),
.BR invf\-fsck (8),
.BR invf\-verify (8)
